# Read by `vite build`, which loads .env.production automatically in production
# mode. Committed on purpose - see the exception in .gitignore.
#
# Every VITE_-prefixed value is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time
# and served to every visitor. That is not a leak to be avoided, it is what the
# prefix means: these are public by construction. Nothing that is not already
# public may be added to this file, and productionEnv.test.ts fails the build if
# a key ever arrives without the prefix or with a secret-shaped name.
#
# The alternative was to set this in Cloudflare Pages' build variables and keep
# the file out of the repository. Rejected: an unset variable does not fail the
# build, it falls back to http://localhost:8080, and the deployed application
# would look perfectly healthy while every request from a real browser failed.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.cyber-half.com